cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below — and please include the firmware version, topology and raw CSV you compared against, not just the conclusion."
title: "Switch 2 Pro Controller (057E:2069) USB 0x05 report field notes"
abstract: >-
  Read-only reverse engineering of the Nintendo Switch 2 Pro Controller's USB HID report 0x05:
  frame layout, a 32-bit 3 MHz-derived clock that wraps every 1,431,655.765 ms, the charge-status
  bitfield, the full charging cycle with its 2.9 Hz chopping maintenance phase, gauge-reading
  semantics, stick travel range, rumble power cost, and a complete 6-axis IMU (accel +/-8 g,
  gyro +/-2000 dps) carried in the same report. All captures come from a single unit; a
  reproduction procedure for other units is included.
